      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:80a5ebfca7dbaa684f232b9b1071ef32c64ee3ee250e7db49fbb1d8cd87e18b3",
      "text": "Scheduled polling periodically retrieves Salesforce changes and must manage successful time windows and repeated processing. Event subscriptions expose change notifications through a persistent transport; CometD long-polling and Pub/Sub pull-based streaming are subscription mechanisms, not scheduled Case queries. Implementation experience reports polling latency and API-limit risks. Subscriptions still need replay state, bounded-outage recovery, and record retrieval for reconciliation. Salesforce also warns that rare CDC publication failures cannot be recovered. These distinctions matter when choosing timely Case alert inputs without assuming event delivery replaces all reads.",
