  "navigation": {
    "schema": "llms-navigation-overrides/v1",
    "ownership": "hand-maintained-with-explicit-regenerator",
    "summary": "Compare centralized incremental reads, subscription transports, retention and recovery limits, and clock-only conditions when choosing a Case ingestion strategy.",
    "facet_notes": {
      "mechanism": "Polling clients should retain the timespan of successful replication, cover all relevant changes even when processing overlaps, and resume consecutive timespans after a failed poll.; Salesforce Pub/Sub Subscribe is a pull-based bidirectional event stream with flow control.; Pub/Sub Subscribe uses a long-lived bidirectional stream with pull-based event demand and flow control. \u2014 3 units",
      "how-to": "Use event subscriptions for prompt change ingestion and retain a reconciliation path for Case alert state when missing changes would matter. This is an architectural inference: Salesforce warns that some change events can be lost unrecoverably. \u2014 1 unit",
      "problems": "On a Subscribe error the long-lived connection stops, and the client must retry Subscribe to establish a new connection.; Salesforce documents a 72-hour retention window for platform and CDC events and does not guarantee retention beyond it.; A Salesforce support article dated June 5, 2026 says CDC cannot emit a change event merely because a non-persisted calculated value changes; it suggests retrieving unsupported values through scheduled Apex queries or an event-triggered read. \u2014 3 units",
      "comparisons": "A published CDC implementation explicitly uses /data/CaseChangeEvent as a Case subscription channel.; Event subscriptions require recovery state: Pub/Sub clients can store a replay ID and resubscribe within the retained event window.; Salesforce explicitly warns that CDC uses distributed-system semantics: in rare cases event messages are not persisted, are not delivered, and cannot be recovered. \u2014 4 units",
      "facts": "Client applications retrieve changed data by polling periodically.; Realtor.com reports that its scheduled Salesforce REST polling risked rate limits and added latency.; CDC does not remove the need for record retrieval. \u2014 4 units"
    },
